{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013909-secrets-of-the-covenants-errata-thread","id":1013909,"title":"Secrets of the Covenants errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-07T12:38:07-08:00","id":1013909,"title":"Secrets of the Covenants errata thread","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/199280/Secrets-of-the-Covenants\" target=\"_blank\">The advance PDF of <i>Secrets of the Covenants </i>is out!</a><br /> <br /> Please use this thread to report any typos or visual glitches. Discussion of content should go to other threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 12-07-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:31:17-08:00","id":1013948,"title":"","content":"P46 'was as little too eager' should be 'was a little too eager'<br /> <br /> P47, 'one of the mortal gunman' should be 'one of the mortal gunmen'<br /> <br /> Also on p47, 'we fled down through entrance we\u2019d build into a storm drain to escape' needs some work. Maybe 'we fled down through entrances we'd built into a storm drain to escape' but 'entrances' for escapes seems a little clunky. Also 'build' should be 'built'.<br /> <br /> And on p47, near the bottom 'her' is in italics in 'inside of her,' and it stands out due to the font and doesn't seem to fit.<br /> <br /> On p33 and p34, there's fairly large spaces where an apostrophe should be in 'when you're waiting to board' also further down in 'I'd have it rough.' and 'I'm a white girl.' The problem continues on the next page with 'what I'm used to,' 'somebody else's problem' and 'I didn't want to duck back,' 'I'd never run before.' 'I shouldn't have been able to make' 'I couldn't attend the celebration,' 'couldn't imagine what that meant.' 'Movement doesn't mobilize' 'Dubai's Movement ruled by Meritocracy,' with a large space between by and Meritocracy. 'If you're strong enough' 'devour someone's soul' 'you're entitled to it.' 'If you're weak,' and' 'Ishaq wasn't'<br /> <br /> In the same section, there's supposed to be a comma or period after 'It makes me aggressive and hungry' but instead is a large space. Same problem later with 'into nothingness, it was as if'<br /> <br /> P57, it seems to say 'USians.' It might be referring to Americans, or misspelled Asians. If the former, the term is not widely known or used and may cause confusion.<br /> <br /> P62, 'leant' should be 'lent.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-08-2016, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:33:13-08:00","id":1013950,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 169: </b>&quot;<b>Where for</b> this cadaverous afterbirth? Had a corruption fermented in <b>is </b>breast&quot; -- <i><b>Wherefore</b></i>, and <b><i>is </i></b>should be <b><i>his</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 192: </b>&quot;Religion is two things to the Lancea et <b>Sanctum; </b>faith and organization.&quot; -- semicolon should be a colon<br /> <br /> <b>p. 196: </b>I think <b>The Guiding Star </b>is supposed to be a 4 dot ritual, unless it's accidentally out of sequence.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 200: </b>&quot;However, you can find other Supernatural Merits in other<b> <i>World </i>of Darkness </b>books.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 2: </b>On a similar note, the copyright boilerplate seems to be the <b>WoD </b>one, rather than the <b>CofD </b>one (though I don't know if that matters; I'm just comparing what's in <b>Hurt Locker</b>). The Onyx Path URL also has <b>backslashes </b>instead of slashes, and it's missing the <b>WWP website</b>.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-07-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:17:11-08:00","id":1013997,"title":"","content":"On page 187, 'Every Contact your character counts as a Skill Specialty' should be 'Every Contact your character has counts as a Skill Specialty'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:26:59-08:00","id":1014005,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 200:</b> &quot;Now, drawbacks do not always occur when using Supernatural Merits granted by this Coil.&quot; -- this seems to refer to something that was cut; I think it was supposed to be in the first dot, but it's not anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:15:22-08:00","id":1014044,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 182:</b> &quot;Mandragoras transplanted from elsewhere wither and die if not cared for by a character with this Merit.&quot; -- Mandragora is already plural (the singular being Mandrake), so the s at the end of &quot;Mandragoras&quot; should be removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T18:40:34-08:00","id":1014085,"title":"","content":"p. 184: The Cruac rituals seem to be out of sequence, unless the order is something I'm not seeing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:11:11-08:00","id":1014094,"title":"","content":"Starting on page 23, the text introduces Ferdinand and Cesar <i>Rodriguez</i>, but the letters they send each other are addressed to Ferdinand and Cesar <i>Araujo</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:16:31-08:00","id":1014116,"title":"","content":"&quot;Cruac Style Merits&quot; and the following fluff is printed twice. Once, and then once again immediately following, starting on page 182.<br /> <br /> This is probably gonna mess with layout a bit as they both take up quite a bit of space.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, on page 179 under the Breaking the Chains Carthian Law reads: &quot; A member of the Movement in good standing can <br /> only take Breaking the Chains.&quot; which i think is meant to read &quot;Only a member of the Movement in good standing can take Breaking the Chains.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 12-07-2016, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T01:50:43-08:00","id":1014211,"title":"","content":"p. 107: &quot;But so many other Kindred <b>died;</b> Kindred with sires, broodmates, and childer in cities all over the nation.&quot; -- semicolon should be a dash or a colon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-11-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T04:24:43-08:00","id":1014242,"title":"","content":"It was specified in the boards by developers that you can use more than one Willpower per turn, as long as you don't use it for the same roll, in 2e, after a clarification request.<br /> <br /> Unleash the Mind (p. 200) allows to spend Willpower more than once per turn, but...you can already do that without the Coil.<br /> I'm sorry I can't provide immediate back up for my claim, but I was pretty surprised when I saw that in the topic. I remember that because I had to change some of the rules of my fangame. I think it was MachineIV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:23:10-08:00","id":1014390,"title":"","content":"In the main page for Invictus: The Game it has:<br /> <br /> Sarah and Mikhail will represent elitism and egalitarianism.<br /> <br /> I think Sarah is the egalitarian from the later text.<br /> <br /> (This might not really be an error, as it doesn't say &quot;Sarah and Mikhail ... respectively&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:55:30-08:00","id":1014402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013909-secrets-of-the-covenants-errata-thread?p=1014242#post1014242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was specified in the boards by developers that you can use more than one Willpower per turn, as long as you don't use it for the same roll, in 2e, after a clarification request.<br /> <br /> Unleash the Mind (p. 200) allows to spend Willpower more than once per turn, but...you can already do that without the Coil.<br /> I'm sorry I can't provide immediate back up for my claim, but I was pretty surprised when I saw that in the topic. I remember that because I had to change some of the rules of my fangame. I think it was MachineIV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger?p=965755#post965755\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...755#post965755</a><br /> <br /> That's David's post, and I think he's mostly talking about instances where you're forced to spend Willpower in a turn. Like, if you have to spend Willpower to do one thing in a turn (like staving off the effect of a supernatural power or Condition), you can still use Willpower on the activation of special abilities. I don't think he means you can add Willpower to an ability you've already spent on to activate (hence the usefulness of this Coil). The rule he's referring to in CofD (p. 73) is that you can't normally spend more than one Willpower on an *action*, so I think it all works out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T13:14:06-08:00","id":1014433,"title":"","content":"Also, being able to do that is explicitly one of the abilities of Horrors. And they can only spend up to their potency on different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T15:05:38-08:00","id":1014464,"title":"","content":"Fine, thank you for the clarification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T15:07:23-08:00","id":1014468,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 112, text around the CD:</b> There's a weird thing that happens depending on what PDF reader you're using. When I use Adobe Reader and the Windows in-built one, the text beneath the CD seems to change fonts from the one above in the narrow column (and from the one on the next page), or at least something odd happens and the text gets rendered differently; in Foxit Reader, there's no problem.<br /> <b>p. 112:</b> &quot;Don\u2019t get me wrong, reading the Testament can be <b>entertaining; </b>but...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 125: </b>&quot;The man rose up, but I bared my fangs at him and <b>hiss</b>...&quot; -- should be <b>hissed</b><br /> <b>p. 135: </b>&quot;Then there was Bonnefil <b>was </b>trying to stab me.&quot;<br /> <b>p. 135: </b>&quot;Leila <b>has </b>some on her face and dress...&quot; -- from context, I think this is supposed to be <b>had</b>.<br /> <b>p. 136: </b>&quot;While there is a certain practicality to consider when one\u2019s faith intersects with the rest of Kindred society that does not belittle or deepen the faith.&quot; -- I think there's a comma missing after <b>society</b><br /> <b>p. 140: </b>&quot;There was no signpost that showed me the best path<b> forward;</b> although my skill and natural talent held me in good stead.&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 140: </b>&quot;...in the years to come. <i><b>That </b></i>is faith.&quot; -- The font is wrong (I think it's supposed to be underlined, rather than italics)<br /> <b>Lancea chapter footer: </b>&quot;Lancea <b>Et </b>Sanctum&quot; -- should be lowercase?<br /> <br /> <b>p. 143: </b>&quot;Let me ask you a <b>question;</b> what...&quot; -- semicolon should be a colon.<br /> <b>p. 144: </b>On the poster, there's an asterisk before &quot;THE MOBIUS STRIP TEASE&quot;; it might be a mistake, or it might be its mate is missing.<br /> <b>p. 144: </b>The &quot;<b>From: discord_scholar&quot;</b> is missing before the first message (though maybe that's intentional)<br /> <b>p. 149: </b>From &quot;<b>R is for Rayna</b>...&quot; to &quot;...<b>it was always open.</b>&quot; The formatting seems to be wrong; I <i>think </i>it's supposed to be the Moroi's voice, not Jacob's.<br /> <b>p. 149: </b>&quot;On further reflection, I am disgusted with the degeneracy into which your childer.&quot; -- there's a word missing?<br /> <b>pp. 152-156: </b>All the apostrophes and quotation marks are hidden. Also, there's a weird glitch with words with Fs followed by L or I, where those characters disappear:<br /> - p. 152: muffled<br /> - p. 153: muffled<br /> - p. 154: mummified<br /> - p. 154: terrified<br /> - p. 154: cornfield<br /> - p. 154: flowed<br /> - p. 155: fingernails<br /> - p. 155: flesh<br /> - p. 155: find<br /> - p. 155: pacified<br /> - p. 155: bonfire<br /> - p. 155: flame<br /> - p. 156: fire<br /> - p. 156: flame<br /> - p. 156: film<br /> - p. 156: flesh<br /> - p. 156: flaming<br /> - p. 156: flinch<br /> <br /> <b>p. 201, sidebar:</b> &quot;To say <b>The </b>Mysteries of the Dragon are imperfect sciences would be a gross understatement.&quot; - should be lowercase?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-09-2016, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:58:47-08:00","id":1014570,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 181:</b> &quot;the Acolyte may cast rituals on her garden that would normally last a scene. The magic of the garden sustains these rituals indefinitely.&quot; There are currently no Cruac rituals in second edition with effects than normally last a scene. Consider changing this to &quot;the Acolyte may cast rituals on her garden that would normally last until sunrise&quot;, as the majority of rituals with lingering effects last for the remainder of the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T20:18:15-08:00","id":1014588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013909-secrets-of-the-covenants-errata-thread?p=1014570#post1014570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Page 181:</b> &quot;the Acolyte may cast rituals on her garden that would normally last a scene. The magic of the garden sustains these rituals indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also suggest changing that to 'rituals in her garden' as most directional rituals are damaging ones and it would give a lot more use to the garden. But less an errata and more a suggestion. Though then you'd have to add in that it would only last as long as you were in the garden, or had it with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-08-2016, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T20:54:05-08:00","id":1014601,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 40:</b> &quot;He had no <b>proof;</b> but...&quot; -- semicolon &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 40:</b> &quot;At least, that\u2019s what his letter <b>said .</b>&quot;<br /> <b>p. 41: </b>&quot;...when I <b>lead </b>the man...&quot; -- should be <b>led<br /> p. 41:</b> &quot;'You have a problem with <b>authority.</b>' <b>He </b>finally suggested...&quot; -- period &gt; comma, and <b>He </b>should be lowercase<br /> <b>p. 42: </b>&quot;...we made <b>love; </b>and...&quot; -- semicolon &gt; comma, or cut the <b>and</b><br /> <b>p. 43: </b>&quot;Because the anger is often righteous and beautiful and the power is <b>sexy; </b>and while...&quot; -- semicolon &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 44: </b>&quot;'...not in here <b>debating.</b>' I muttered...&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 44: </b>&quot;I followed his <b>gestured</b>...&quot;<br /> <b>p. 47: </b>The Sanctified Paladins are called &quot;<b>Templars</b>&quot; a couple times; that might just be an alternate name, rather than an error, but I was a little confused at first because the action is set inside a Circle of the Crone <i>temple</i>.<br /> <b>p. 47:</b> &quot;We stood <b>outside </b>of the place, the Paladins still screaming from <b>outside</b>.&quot; -- the second <i>outside </i>should be <b>inside</b>?<br /> <b>p. 47: </b>The transition between the burnt paper fragments at the bottom of the page is awkward, and breaks the flow of the sentence (&quot;...in embers, and / whatever it...&quot;)<br /> <b>p. 55: </b>&quot;'I didn't want to bother you with <b>it.</b>' <b>She </b>told me...&quot; -- period &gt; comma, and <b>She </b>should be lowercase<br /> <b>p. 55: </b>&quot;'You don't have to do this <b>alone.</b>' I told her.&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 56: </b>&quot;...and <b>watch </b>the hibiscus slam itself into my window.&quot; -- should be <b>watched<br /> p. 58:</b> &quot;The thing is <b>though;</b> you need shit to grow good produce&quot; -- semicolon &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 58:</b> &quot;If you can mumble in an old language, <b>read </b>simple omens, or better yet, <b>read </b>them<b>; </b>so many will treat you as a seer&quot; -- I think the second <i>read </i>is supposed to be a different word, and the semicolon should be a comma.<br /> <b>p. 60: </b>&quot;'It\u2019s a tricky <b>thing.</b>' Michael asked...&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 60: </b>&quot;...but one I do correspond <b>with an expert.</b>&quot; -- missing an <b>is </b>before <i>expert </i>(or cut the <b>one</b>?)<br /> <b>p. 60: </b>&quot;...<b>it seemed logical</b> that when the disturbances to the Kindred of Nasiriyah began, in the way that they began, <b>it was logical</b> I should be the one brought in.&quot;<br /> <b>p. 60: </b>&quot;...while <b>those </b><b>Spear,</b> (Islamic, I make note for you, <b>cousin,</b>)&quot; -- the first comma isn't needed, and the second should come after the parenthesis. <i>Those</i> <i>Spear</i> should also be something like &quot;those of the Spear&quot; (or maybe just &quot;those Spears&quot;)?<br /> <b>p. 61:</b> &quot;...several members of <b>society </b>saw a false sun...&quot; -- missing a <b>the</b><br /> <b>p. 61: </b>&quot;'I have no need of <b>lies.</b>' <b>He </b>said...&quot; -- period &gt; comma, and <b>He </b>should be lowercase<br /> <br /> <b>p. 157: </b>&quot;The first Mekhet were all like <b>you; </b>but what was once...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 165: </b>&quot;The poor <b>savaged </b>tried to pull away...&quot;<br /> <b>pp. 171-174: </b>Are there supposed to be headers for the journal entries?<br /> <br /> <b>p. 178: </b>&quot;...a first level Mystery of the Dragon, a Theban <b>Sorcery, </b>or Cr\u00faac ritual, or an Invictus Merit...&quot; -- the comma there makes the list read strangely, or it should say &quot;Miracle&quot; after Sorcery<br /> <b>p. 179: </b>&quot;She must feed from <b>\u2013and </b>thus...&quot; -- needs a space after the dash<br /> <b>pp. 179-180: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">&quot;</span></span>...become an additional Dirge for the <b>character; </b>thus allowing...&quot; -- semicolon &gt; comma","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-09-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T05:26:20-08:00","id":1014715,"title":"","content":"page 65: &quot;Jerome and Jewel sit stiffly, looking at the \ufb02oor, showing not the wisdom to watch the Genius as he speaks in order to glean what lessons they can from his words. Jewel is in her mid-twenties, with <b>deep skin</b> and honey-brown eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Deep what skin?<br /> <br /> page 68: &quot;<i>Jerome reaches over and takes his sister's hand</i>.&quot; does not make it completely clear that Jerome is now the one speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-09-2016, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:23:16-08:00","id":1014991,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 3: </b>There are two entries for Cruac Style Merits, as per the doubling on 182.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 6: </b>The font used for the handwritten notes on the bottom and right-side of the page (&quot;<b>The French Movement...</b>&quot; and &quot;<b>Sorry to my...</b>&quot;) has that thing where the apostrophes are invisible<br /> <b>p. 11:</b> &quot;Lieu Hanh kept French Kindred <b>advisors, locals</b> viewed outsiders as mostly dangerous.&quot; -- needs an <b>and</b>, I think? (or a semicolon)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 62: </b>&quot;'What do you know about them?' <b>He </b>scoffed...&quot; -- lowercase<br /> <b>p. 62</b><b>:</b> &quot;'We'll need to <b>move.</b>' I said.&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 62</b><b>: </b>&quot;'Get over <b>yourself.</b>' I told him...&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 63: </b>&quot;...and <b>lead </b>Michael past the kine...&quot; -- <b>led</b><br /> <b>p. 63: </b>&quot;'Your cult, you <b>mean,</b>' <b>he </b>watched me...&quot; -- comma should be a period; <i>he </i>should be uppercase.<br /> <b>p. 63: </b>&quot;'What do you know about her?' with a touch of fear...&quot; -- there's a <b>he said </b>missing, I think.<br /> <b>p. 63: &quot;</b>'...her name is Mae.' I told him...&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 64: </b>&quot;'...Don\u2019t be <b>foolish.</b>' I snapped at him.&quot; -- period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 64:</b> &quot;'You're a monster!' <b>He </b>told me again.&quot; -- lowercase<br /> <b>p. 64: </b>&quot;'...never been there <b>myself.</b>\u201d Michael said...&quot; period &gt; comma<br /> <b>p. 64: </b>&quot;I shook <b>her </b>head.&quot; -- <b>my</b><br /> <b>p. 65:</b> The paragraph that starts <b>&quot;As always, our great Genius...&quot;</b> -- I think this is supposed to be in italics, like the narrator's other sections; it doesn't seem to be part of the dialogue above<br /> <b>p. 66: </b>&quot;<i><b>sneering</b></i>&quot; -- I think this is supposed to be in the header above, like the other &quot;stage directions&quot;?<br /> <b>p. 66:</b> &quot;I suppose the most important question is<b> this; </b>do you...&quot; -- semicolon should be a colon<br /> <b>p. 66: </b>&quot;The <b>Axes\u2019 </b>warning pins the Acolyte...&quot; -- should be <b>Axe's </b>(it doesn't seem to be multiple people, from later context)<br /> <b>p. 66: </b>&quot;At that point, <b>began the twins</b> telling their story.&quot; -- should be <b>the twins began</b>? (might be intended to be the narrator's odd cadence, though)<br /> <b>p. 67: </b>&quot;...and speaks in whispers <b>to elder</b>.&quot; -- missing a <b>the</b><br /> <b>p. 68: </b>There's a &quot;<b>Jerome</b>&quot; dialogue header missing above &quot;<i>Jerome reaches over...</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 70: </b>&quot;...you are <b>it;</b> for you will...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 70: </b>The footer is a bit hard to see against the white paper<br /> <b>p. 71: </b>&quot;Especially now <b>\u2014business</b> is booming...&quot; -- should be a space after the dash<br /> <b>p. 71: </b>&quot;...which, in turn, <b>lead </b>them to Veronica.&quot; -- <b>led</b><br /> <b>p. 72: </b>&quot;There are tricks for that; but to be honest...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 77: </b>The text on the left scrap is bleeding onto the right scrap where it says &quot;silk.&quot;<br /> <b>p. 79: </b>&quot;...to go behind the Princess\u2019 back, but <b>surely</b>...&quot; -- the word is in the wrong font<br /> <b>p. 80</b><b>: </b>&quot;...and <b>me </b>in Belfast, but our minds are still one. <b>Therefore</b>...&quot; -- &quot;me&quot; and &quot;Therefore&quot; aren't in the same font as the surrounding text<br /> <b>p. 81: </b>&quot;Of <b>course</b>, we must never question...&quot; -- Same font thing as p. 80.<br /> <b>p. 84: </b>The footer is white on white with the page; looks off<br /> <b>p. 85: </b>&quot;Girl looks terrible by the <b>way</b>...&quot; -- wrong font again<br /> <b>p. 88: </b>&quot;She said that '<b>they</b>'...&quot; -- wrong font<br /> <b>p. 89:</b> &quot;...but they too fell; wiped out on...&quot; -- semicolon should be a colon or a dash<br /> <b>p. 89: </b>&quot;Sophia Goldstein is the Invictus <b>electorate </b>of Berlin...&quot; -- should be <b>elector</b><br /> <b>p. 93: </b>&quot;...the city, <b>its </b>people...&quot; -- wrong font<br /> <b>p. 93: </b>&quot;...Kindred suffer from <b>rst </b>stage Krokodil...&quot; -- the F followed by I glitch again<br /> <b>p. 93: </b>&quot;<b>\u2013 I </b>made her show <b>me \u2013</b>&quot; -- both those dashes are invisible in the pdf<br /> <b>p. 94: </b>&quot;The names on it are <b>real \u2013 all</b> lost Kindred...&quot; -- another invisible dash<br /> <b>p. 96: </b>&quot;Creepy as<b> hell; </b>but...&quot; semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 96:</b> &quot;...she didn\u2019t <b>appreciated </b>her/our sire...&quot;<br /> <b>p. 97: </b>The footer is behind the text, and not very visible. It seems to get lost a lot in this chapter (next page too; is there supposed to be a black outline around the footer text?)<br /> <b>p. 98: </b>&quot;<b>Beatrice: But </b>it fell.&quot; -- The space after the colon should be a tab<br /> <b>p. 98: </b>&quot;...we transformed along with the <b>timse</b>.&quot;<br /> <b>p. 100:</b> &quot;...still sleeps under the <b>[blanked out]</b>...&quot; -- I think this is supposed to actually be blanked out? It seems odd that the narrator would write that in cursive handwriting, in her diary (there are instances of <b>[blanked out]</b> in Beatrice's transcripts too, so maybe they're all supposed to be obscured?)<br /> <b>pp. 100-101, transcript: Gennaro </b>becomes<b> Professor Gennaro</b> in the dialogue, and it breaks the alignment of the formatting<br /> <b>p. 105: </b>&quot;...disappointed to see them <b>go</b>.&quot; -- wrong font<br /> <br /> <b>Bookmarks: </b>There aren't any bookmarks for &quot;The Trouble with Carmilla&quot; (p. 77) or &quot;Facility 52&quot; (p. 91)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-13-2016, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:58:17-08:00","id":1015395,"title":"","content":"p. 194: <b>Temple of Damnation</b> should include as a Prerequisite Lancea et Sanctum Status \u2022.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T23:46:01-08:00","id":1015573,"title":"","content":"P77, text convo: Mikhail's last reply is part of Sarah's bubble<br /> <br /> P80 bottom &amp; P81 top: Same email convo repeated<br /> <br /> P93 &quot;suffer from rst stage&quot; should be &quot;suffer from first stage&quot;<br /> <br /> P98 &quot;Beatrice: But it fell&quot; is not indented<br /> <br /> P100 &quot;sleeps under the [blanked out]&quot; looks kinda weird since it's a handwritten document. Maybe put a location there (ie the Colosseum) and black it like they do in redacted government docs.<br /> <br /> P100: The interview starts between &quot;Gennaro&quot; and Beatrice, then switches to &quot;Professor Gennaro&quot;. For indentation's sake maybe stick to Gennaro, even if that means the transcriber improperly dropped his title.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T00:27:45-08:00","id":1015585,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 14:</b> &quot;While a couple of licks put forward the idea that maybe, just maybe, the Embrace should be <b>limited;</b> the ruling council...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 19:</b> &quot;This is doubly <b>nice;</b> because...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 21:</b> &quot;...than feeling <b>good;</b> and...&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma<br /> <b>p. 23, sidebar:</b> The apostrophe in the &quot;I'm&quot; of the header is invisible.<br /> <b>p. 25:</b> &quot;<b>Our sire? Caridad de Flores?</b>&quot; -- wrong font<br /> <b>p. 33-34:</b> Some of the apostrophes and dashes are invisible in the Dubai story font<br /> <b>p. 37:</b> &quot;...I'd <b><i>love</i></b> to see...&quot; -- wrong font<br /> <br /> <b>p. 180:</b> &quot;...<b>needs possess</b> this Merit.&quot; -- missing a &quot;to&quot;<br /> <b>p. 181: </b>&quot;When the Movement conquered <b>Honolulu</b>...&quot; -- the Crone chapter seems to indicate it's an Acolyte city? I might be misreading it.<br /> <b>p. 181: </b>The first column on the right hand side of the page is out of alignment with the ones under it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-18-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T10:24:03-08:00","id":1016149,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 8: </b>&quot;<b>Mayor Blasio</b>.&quot; \u2014 The name of New York's mayor is Bill <b>de Blasio</b>.<br /> <b>p. 199: &quot;</b>Characters inside a chapterhouse are <b>calmed and collected</b>.&quot; \u2014 The idiom is &quot;calm and collected.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/201-jadasc","user":"Jadasc","date":". 12-12-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/201-jadasc","name":"Jadasc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:46:31-08:00","id":1016285,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 118:</b> The star and connected note is in an awkward place and likely belongs a couple lines higher, where it would align with the end of a sentence. Also, further down, where the text says: &quot;She smiled <b>at me. \u201cWell, if</b> we're seen together&quot;, the bolded parts are in a different font from the surrounding text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T23:21:50-08:00","id":1016421,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 184: </b>&quot;...only one such monster will be present at a given<b> time; </b>no matter how many times the vampire uses Cr\u00faac.&quot; -- semicolon should be a comma (or a dash)<br /> <b>p. 192: </b>Not exactly a mistake, but the Lancea et Sanctum section doesn't get a nifty subtitle in the heading or the page footer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-13-2016, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T05:39:22-08:00","id":1016505,"title":"","content":"pp. 152-156<br /> <br /> The font used is difficult for me to read. I don't know if that applies to anyone else, but I thought I'd mention. A specific thing that I find very difficult to interpret is &quot;room number #&quot; and the # is basically unreadable. Maybe that's intended. It's not 9, which is the number it most closely resembles.<br /> <br /> Also, it looks like words that start with &quot;F&quot; in this section lose their first two letters. I saw &quot; nd&quot; for &quot;find,&quot; &quot; ame&quot; for &quot;flame,&quot; &quot; re&quot; for &quot;fire,&quot; but there may be others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T05:53:51-08:00","id":1016506,"title":"","content":"Copy-pasting the number makes it turn up as a 9 in other fonts. But I do agree that the font is difficult to read.<br /> <br /> Other symbols that for some reason doesn't show up is all the apostrophes throughout the entire text, as far as I checked, as well as the bolded letters in this line on page 152:<br /> &quot;Then we were on the road. And a muf<b>fl</b>ed voice from the box said, \u201cThat wasn<b>\u2019</b>t funny.&quot;&quot;<br /> <br /> The omission of apostrophes might be intentional if the writer isn't supposed to be proficient with English, but I doubt it, and either way they still leave unnatural spaces in the middle of words.<br /> <br /> Edit: All of which Yossarian already had pointed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T06:05:33-08:00","id":1016509,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah, I scanned for it before I posted but I didn't spot it in Yossarian's post. Thanks btw, for some reason copy-pasting didn't cross my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:36:18-08:00","id":1016683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013909-secrets-of-the-covenants-errata-thread?p=1016506#post1016506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copy-pasting the number makes it turn up as a 9 in other fonts. But I do agree that the font is difficult to read.<br /> <br /> Other symbols that for some reason doesn't show up is all the apostrophes throughout the entire text, as far as I checked, as well as the bolded letters in this line on page 152:<br /> &quot;Then we were on the road. And a muf<b>fl</b>ed voice from the box said, \u201cThat wasn<b>\u2019</b>t funny.&quot;&quot;<br /> <br /> The omission of apostrophes might be intentional if the writer isn't supposed to be proficient with English, but I doubt it, and either way they still leave unnatural spaces in the middle of words.<br /> <br /> Edit: All of which Yossarian already had pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scripty fonts can get squirrelly with punctuation sometimes, especially &quot;curly&quot; quotation marks / apostrophes, and dashes...but that F+I/L thing is <i>super </i>weird. It does it somewhere else, too, in a different font, which is even weirder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-13-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:48:29-08:00","id":1016778,"title":"","content":"P. 149: